---
// The Lumit wordmark - a transcription of the owner's After Effects reference.
// Per-frame position, rotation, thickness and arm lengths are sampled off the
// 50-frame render (skeleton extraction, verified by overlay); the right
// keyframe is the same sampled motion flipped 180 degrees about the lockup's centre,
// exactly as the AE project flips its precomp.
//
// Each keyframe is ONE path, so there is no seam where the arms meet. Corner
// treatment per the owner: the L's top-left and bottom-right corners are sharp,
// everything else rounds (w/2 caps, 0.35w inner elbow); the t inherits the same
// two sharp corners through the flip. Gradients are userSpaceOnUse over the
// letter's local box so the colour runs continuously across both arms; the
// right element's stops are reversed so the flipped t reads violet at its top.
//
// The green is on the L and the blue on the flipped t - the two arms swapped
// families, so the lockup opens green and closes blue. The blue is the same
// cyan-to-blue it always was; the green replaces a violet-to-pink, which was
// the accent's own family and went with it.
//
// No tittle - the t's overhang owns the i's dot position.
//
// The glow rides the diamond exactly: its scale is a fixed multiple of the
// diamond's radius, so the two grow and leave together. Drawn over everything.
//
// The animation holds the rest pose 100ms, then runs. The launch is
// stretched 300ms with a power
// ramp that starts near-still and meets the reference's own speed exactly at
// the apex; from there the motion plays 1:1 until the snap home, which is
// re-timed to accelerate into rest (about 1260ms total). Without script, or
// under reduced motion, the markup is the finished wordmark standing still.
interface Props { class?: string }
const { class: klass } = Astro.props;
---

